# CFOperator trial configuration — copy to .env and edit.
# Only the first block genuinely matters; everything else has a default.

# ── Required: the three values ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. An LLM. Either a local Ollama…
OLLAMA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
#    …or leave Ollama unreachable and set a paid key as the working provider:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# 2. Your Prometheus (host.docker.internal = the machine running compose).
PROMETHEUS_URL=http://host.docker.internal:9090

# 3. Where to notify (optional but recommended — this is how you SEE triage).
#    Any subset; a blank value leaves that sink off rather than half-configured.
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── Optional observability ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOKI_URL=http://host.docker.internal:3100
# ALERTMANAGER_URL=http://host.docker.internal:9093

# ── `cfoperator init --non-interactive` ──────────────────────────────────────
# The wizard answers its interview from the variables above — it probes each
# one and then writes config.yaml + .env, so CI and the demo drive the same
# path a human takes. These three are the only knobs it does not read from a
# variable something else already uses; each has a default, so an unset one is
# a silent choice rather than an error, which is why they are named here.
#
# Which provider the wizard configures. Unset means ollama, which reads
# OLLAMA_URL + OLLAMA_MODEL above; any other value (groq, xai, gemini,
# anthropic) makes it require that provider's <NAME>_API_KEY instead.
# CFOP_INIT_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
#
# Model for a non-ollama provider (ollama uses OLLAMA_MODEL). Blank = the
# provider's own default.
# CFOP_INIT_LLM_MODEL=
#
# How much CFOperator is allowed to do: investigate | remediate. Unset means
# investigate — read-only. `--profile` on the command line wins over this.
# CFOP_INIT_PROFILE=investigate

# ── Optional overrides (sane defaults otherwise) ─────────────────────────────
# Console admin. If CFOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD is unset, one is generated and printed
# once in `docker compose logs bootstrap`. `cfoperator init` writes these two
# for you; first boot seeds the console account from them.
# CFOP_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
# CFOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Host port for the console. Change it if 8083 is already in use.
# CFOP_CONSOLE_PORT=8083

# Bundled Postgres credentials (internal to the compose network).
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=cfoperator
# POSTGRES_DB=cfoperator
# POSTGRES_USER=cfoperator

# Signs console session cookies. The compose bootstrap generates and persists
# one automatically, so leave this unset unless you want to pin your own —
# nothing is generated per-process, and an unset secret makes login fail with
# a 500 rather than degrade.
# CFOP_SESSION_SECRET=

# More LLM fallback keys
# XAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Advanced (not needed for the trial; see docs) ────────────────────────────
# GitHub — required only for the remediation PR loop (profile: remediate).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# event_runtime HTTP surface: bearer token for POST /alert and the /history,
# /activity, /scheduled, /jobs read endpoints. In the trial compose the port is
# not published, so unset (open inside the compose network) is acceptable.
# CFOP_RUNTIME_TOKEN=

# Telemetry TimescaleDB (optional) — enables the `timescale_query` tool and the
# mqtt-top-talkers skill. Without TIMESCALE_PASSWORD the tool is not registered.
# Point TIMESCALE_USER at a read-only role; the tool also forces a read-only
# transaction and rejects anything that isn't a single SELECT/WITH.
# TIMESCALE_HOST=
# TIMESCALE_PORT=5432
# TIMESCALE_DB=sensors
# TIMESCALE_USER=cfoperator_ro
# TIMESCALE_PASSWORD=

# Per-service bearer token. In production each service mounts its OWN token
# from auth_api_tokens as this variable; the shared credential that used to
# live here was retired 2026-08-09. The trial compose mints the event-runtime
# token automatically at first boot — do NOT set it here; setting it in the
# agent's own env re-enables a shared credential that belongs to no user and
# cannot be revoked individually. Mint per-service tokens at /tokens.
# CFOP_API_TOKEN=

# Opens the console entirely. Local development only — logs a loud warning.
# CFOP_AUTH_DISABLED=
